WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.730
- Now y'all have met before, right?

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:03.810
You've met, right?

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.770
- We met.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.650
- We met when I was pregnant
with one of my kids.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:08.483
- Yeah.

00:00:08.483 --> 00:00:09.330
- [Kate] I think four years ago.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.500
Yeah, four years ago.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.333
- [Jane] Four years ago.

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:12.166
You were very pregnant.

00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:13.128
- [Kate] Very.

00:00:13.128 --> 00:00:14.610
(chuckles)

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.520
- You always love the
part when they get out

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.510
I love them more.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.090
So, Dr. Jane, when did the love

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.860
of animals like first overwhelm you,

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.180
like, overpower you to where you felt

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.910
like this had to be your life?

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.320
- Well, apparently when I popped out

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.280
of my mother's womb.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.113
- There you go.

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:31.560
Coming back to it.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.780
You just were, from a
child, just obsessed.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.830
Just loved animals.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.160
- Yeah. I mean, I was 18 months old

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.420
and mom came into my room

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.720
and I got this whole handful
of earthworms in my bed

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.730
and she said, "you were looking at them

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.708
so you wondered how do
they walk without legs?"

00:00:48.708 --> 00:00:49.541
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:51.037
- And so she just quietly said

00:00:51.037 --> 00:00:53.790
"let's put them back in the
garden or they might die."

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.400
So, she supported me from the very start.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.390
- That's a beautiful thing.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.857
Because lots of people
would come in and go,

00:00:59.857 --> 00:01:01.507
"what are you doing?"

00:01:01.507 --> 00:01:03.540
- "Throw those dirty
things out. How dare you?"

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:04.530
Yeah.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.640
- But they are very cool.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.870
I'm with you on that.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.330
What was the moment you knew
you had to dedicate your life

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.250
to working with chimpanzees?

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.010
- Well, first of all, it was Africa.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.650
I read "Tarzan of the Apes"
and fell in love with him.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.483
- Yeah.

00:01:17.483 --> 00:01:21.005
- And I was very jealous,
he married the wrong Jane.

00:01:21.005 --> 00:01:22.986
(laughing)

00:01:22.986 --> 00:01:23.819
- He really did.

00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:25.080
- Yeah, he really did.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.050
So, that was when my
dream of Africa began.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.630
I grow up, go to Africa,
live with wild animals

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.250
and write books about them.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.807
And everybody loved except again, mom,

00:01:34.807 --> 00:01:36.930
"If you really want to
do something like this,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.190
you'll have to work really hard.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:40.500
Take advantage of every opportunity.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.990
And if you don't get up,
hopefully you find a way".

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.570
Which I've spread that around the world,

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.630
especially in disadvantaged
communities, you know?

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.847
And so many people have
said, "Jane, thank you.

00:01:50.847 --> 00:01:53.130
You taught me because
you followed your dream.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.960
I can follow mine."

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.610
So anyway, I got out there--
- Absolutely.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:57.443
It's inspiring.

00:01:57.443 --> 00:01:59.670
- Yes. I met Dr. Leakey.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.640
I would've studied any
animal to be in nature

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.830
and he offered me the one most like us.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.400
Like, I mean, it's like fate, isn't it?

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.420
It was meant to be.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.120
And so chimpanzees, I was sent off

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.080
to be the first person
ever to study chimpanzees.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:16.913
- That's incredible.

00:02:16.913 --> 00:02:19.980
So, did you have anything
you wanted to ask Dr. Jane?

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.790
- No, I just I hope I can
be a mom like your mom was.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.680
It's really inspiring because all

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.390
of the things that you said, it's true.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.917
Like our instincts are to go,

00:02:29.917 --> 00:02:31.800
"Oh, don't do that. It's messy."

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.770
But in reality, all of
those little things,

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.500
they really do form a person.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.840
- So you discovered chimpanzees use tools,

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.520
which changed everything really.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.170
So do you remember that moment?

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.643
- Oh yes, of course.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:49.290
I was walking through a
little trail in the forest

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.660
and I saw the first chimpanzee

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.720
who'd begun to lose his
fear of me, David Greybeard,

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:58.740
and he was using grass
stems to fish for termites.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.960
And it was really exciting.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.640
- That's really--
- At that time,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.810
it was thought that humans

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.660
and only humans used and made tools.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.000
Now of course we know other animals do.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:09.833
- Absolutely.

00:03:09.833 --> 00:03:11.640
Of course, humans thought
we were the only ones.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:12.810
- Yeah.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.310
- Look, there's a lot
of great things about us

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:15.810
but there's some not so great.

